title: Make `pallet-assets` transfers move exactly the requested amount

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet_assets::prep_debit` increases a debit to the account's whole balance when debiting the
    requested amount exactly would strand a remainder below the asset's `min_balance`. That is
    sound where the caller can observe it, `fungibles::Balanced::withdraw` reports the promoted
    figure in the credit it returns, and `burn` destroys what it takes and squares supply — but
    at least three consumers could not, and each lost track of the difference:

    - `transfer_and_die` (so `transfer`, `transfer_keep_alive`, `force_transfer`,
      `transfer_approved`, and the `ERC20` precompile) fed the increased debit into `prep_credit`,
      so the destination received `amount + remainder`. For `transfer_approved` this moved more
      of the owner's funds than the allowance the owner had granted, while charging only `amount`
      against that allowance.
    - The default `fungibles::Mutate::transfer` pairs a `BestEffort` `decrease_balance` with an
      `increase_balance` of `amount` and discards the amount actually debited. The remainder left
      the source without being credited anywhere or deducted from `Asset::supply`, so total
      issuance drifted above the sum of all balances. This is the path XCM's `FungiblesAdapter`
      and other pallets take.
    - `pallet_asset_conversion`'s `withdraw` helper resolves the whole returned credit into the
      pool while pricing the swap on the `amount_in` it asked for, so an expendable
      `swap_exact_tokens_for_tokens` paid the remainder into the pool for nothing in return.

    Fixes, none of which change any public signature or require a migration:

    - `transfer_and_die` now requires the debit to equal `amount` unless the caller passed
      `best_effort` or `burn_dust`, returning the new `Error::WouldSweepDust` otherwise. With
      `burn_dust` the destination is still credited exactly `amount` and the remainder is burned,
      which the `burned` balance-change callback reports. Sending the whole
      balance leaves no remainder and still reaps the account. A self-transfer is held to the
      same rule: it moves nothing, but used to report the increased debit as the amount
      transferred, in `Transferred`, in the balance-change callback, and so in the precompile's
      ERC-20 `Transfer` log.
    - `pallet-assets` now implements `fungibles::Mutate::transfer` itself, deferring to
      `do_transfer` after running the same preconditions as the default implementation so the
      same `TokenError`s still surface. Debit and credit are settled against one figure and
      supply stays consistent. Unlike the default, it does not short-circuit a self-transfer, so
      one now emits `Transferred` and runs the balance-change callback like `do_transfer` does,
      and fails with `WouldSweepDust` where any other transfer would.
    - `pallet_asset_conversion::withdraw` rejects an expendable withdrawal that would strand a
      remainder before touching state, and asserts the returned credit matches the requested
      value as a backstop.

    The assets ERC-20 precompile and the asset-conversion precompile also now revert, with a reason a
    contract can read, for the caller-facing failures that used to trap with empty return data.
    `Error::Error` remains only for charging failures, which still arrive through
    `From<DispatchError>`. Other precompiles are unchanged.

    Asset-conversion quotes no longer share "Pool does not exist or has no liquidity". A zero
    amount reverts with "Amount can't be zero", a pair with no pool with "Pool does not exist",
    a created pool with no liquidity with "Pool exists but has no liquidity", and a quote the
    reserves cannot fill with "Insufficient liquidity". `getReserves` uses that same mapping, so
    a missing pool now reports "Pool does not exist" rather than the empty-pool reason.

    Telling those two apart reads `AssetConversion::Pools`, which `WeightInfo::get_reserves` does
    not cover. `pallet-asset-conversion` gains `Pallet::pool_exists` and a matching
    `WeightInfo::pool_exists` benchmark, and the precompile charges it before the read, only when
    the reserves come back empty. Runtimes implementing `pallet_asset_conversion::WeightInfo` must
    add `pool_exists`.

- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Transferring an amount that would leave you holding less than an asset's minimum balance now
    fails with `WouldSweepDust` instead of quietly moving your entire balance, including when you
    send to yourself. This applies to `transfer`, `transfer_keep_alive`, `force_transfer` and
    `transfer_approved`, to ERC-20
    `transfer`/`transferFrom` on `pallet-assets` tokens, to assets moved over XCM, and to
    `swap_exact_tokens_for_tokens` / `swap_tokens_for_exact_tokens` with `keep_alive: false`. Send
    your whole balance instead — that leaves no remainder and still cleans up the account.

    Contracts calling the assets ERC-20 precompile or the asset-conversion precompile should catch
    `Error(string)` for these failures. They used to trap, so `catch Error(string)` never ran and
    the return data was empty:

    - `DELEGATECALL` now reverts with "illegal to call this pre-compile via delegate call".
    - `STATICCALL` of `transfer`, `approve`, `transferFrom`, `permit`, or a state-changing
      asset-conversion method now reverts with "cannot modify state in a static call".
    - `quoteExactTokensForTokens` and `quoteTokensForExactTokens` now say which failure it was:
      "Amount can't be zero", "Pool does not exist", "Pool exists but has no liquidity", or
      "Insufficient liquidity". `getReserves` reports the same pool reasons.
    - A swap that would have to withdraw more than the quoted amount, from the sender or from a
      pool, reverts with "Swap amount cannot be withdrawn exactly". Other calls that hit the same
      token error, such as `removeLiquidity` paying less than the minimum balance to a new
      account, revert with "Account cannot exist with the funds that would be given".

    No storage migration and no signature change. Update any caller that matched the old empty
    return data, or the single quote string "Pool does not exist or has no liquidity".

crates:
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: major
# `WeightInfo` gains `pool_exists`, which every implementor must add.
- name: pallet-asset-conversion
  bump: major
- name: pallet-assets-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-asset-conversion-precompiles
  bump: patch
# Implements the new `pallet_asset_conversion::WeightInfo::pool_exists`.
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
